    {
      "text": "path length to O(n/r). We plan to investigate this approach further in future work.",
      "section_id": "sec:background",
      "page_start": 2,
      "page_end": 8
    },
    {
      "text": "A single convolutional layer with kernel width k < n does not connect all pairs of input and output",
      "section_id": "sec:background",
      "page_start": 2,
      "page_end": 8
    },
    {
      "text": "positions. Doing so requires a stack of O(n/k) convolutional layers in the case of contiguous kernels,",
      "section_id": "sec:background",
      "page_start": 2,
      "page_end": 8
    },
    {
      "text": "or O(logk(n)) in the case of dilated convolutions [18], increasing the length of the longest paths",
      "section_id": "sec:background",
      "page_start": 2,
      "page_end": 8
    },
    {
      "text": "considerably, to O(k · n · d + n · d2). Even with k = n, however, the complexity of a separable",
      "section_id": "sec:background",
      "page_start": 2,
      "page_end": 8
    },
    {
      "text": "We used the Adam optimizer [20] with β1 = 0.9, β2 = 0.98 and ϵ = 10−9. We varied the learning",
      "section_id": "sec:background",
      "page_start": 2,
      "page_end": 8
    },
    {
      "text": "lrate = d−0.5",
      "section_id": "sec:background",
      "page_start": 2,
      "page_end": 8
    },
    {
      "text": "warmup_steps = 4000.",
      "section_id": "sec:background",
      "page_start": 2,
      "page_end": 8
    },
    {
      "text": "Pdrop = 0.1.",
      "section_id": "sec:model",
      "page_start": 8,
      "page_end": 8
    },
    {
      "text": "During training, we employed label smoothing of value ϵls = 0.1 [36]. This",
      "section_id": "sec:model",
      "page_start": 8,
